{"kind":"assert","text":"Case-C review finding for #20301: qualify the impossibility claim before asking Hugh to choose.\n\nThe [candidate note](notes/2026-09-07-previous-frontier-readers.md@7628c518bb2fffab2597f0084f220f4dc642981c:48) says there is no fourth situation and that a retained head which is an ancestor of the current ref necessarily implies an incremental read. A paired isolated probe of exact7628c518 contradicts that absolute claim. The source path is [kernel load followed by witness persistence](internal/app/app.go@7628c518bb2fffab2597f0084f220f4dc642981c:2557): the kernel reader has already advanced before rememberVerifiedFrontier can refuse publication. The retained application snapshot and reader can therefore differ after a real storage failure.\n\nBoth probe arms start with a verified snapshot A. Another workspace appends B. A temporary config-file obstruction causes the resident's witness write to fail after its reader verifies B, leaving the previously published snapshot A and persisted witness A unchanged. After restoring that fixture file, the fixture ref is moved back to A and another valid event C is appended. A is an ancestor of C. With a valid signed checkpoint available, the read uses the checkpoint and correctly emits no cold progress. With both checkpoint selectors absent, the same reader reports Started=true during a cold full audit while retaining same-profile A, then successfully verifies and publishes C. The test observes the retained snapshot inside the actual kernel progress gate before publication. No internal reader, projection or profile field is assigned by the probe.\n\n[Paired result](casec-witness-probe-result.json): both controls pass, package3.606s (individual arms1.71s and1.56s). [Runnable probe](casec-witness-probe_test.go) creates all refs, actors, configuration and checkpoint selectors inside temporary test repositories. It changes no live workroom ref, witness, custody, key, process or telemetry. These are tiny correctness fixtures, not a performance measurement or deployed-reader acceptance.\n\nThis finding does not establish permission or safety to expose A during an unverifiable read. Git ancestry alone is still insufficient, and successful final verification in the fixture is not knowledge the endpoint has before that verification. It also does not establish demand for a new endpoint. Recommendation A may remain the simplest defensible choice, but should be justified by its verification contract, supported failure states, expected benefit and maintenance cost, rather than the assertion that the retained-ancestor state cannot occur. Check the seven-rule alternative against reader/projection separation and publication failures explicitly. Remove or substantiate the note's unmeasured claim that tail verification is ordinarily sub-second at this workroom depth and rarely long.\n\nPlease address this within the live20301 commitment and independent review15491dfc. If the note changes, publish the corrected exact head and request fresh review; preserve the full case-C implementation-if-adopted or explicit-decline-plus-guidance outcome. Proposal74943d8f is pending; this finding neither adopts nor declines it, and design review is not final case-C completion.","body":{"head":"7628c518bb2fffab2597f0084f220f4dc642981c","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:15491dfc4898fc5db7c34342c65e55b05a1ba17c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:33c335a14da70a7b2077bdb77b7527508188b550 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:012451209d3000492d2e523089e5973beec05f61, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015aba51ab6c2416861618c5ac3c9ae0e444f17f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f and 125 more","to":"hugh"}}